{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_c1fc78cebe69939bc23a4adb","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"kimi-k2.7-code","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Root cause**\n\n`config-cache.mjs` stored the in-flight `Promise` in the cache `Map` before it settled. When the origin rejected, that rejected promise stayed in the map, so every later `getConfig(\"acme\")` found a “cache hit,” awaited the same rejection, and returned the original timeout. The cache was correctly coalescing concurrent misses, but it was also permanently caching failures.\n\nLog evidence:\n- `cfg-781` is a `cache=miss` `503 origin_timeout`.\n- The next line is an origin probe `200` in 31 ms — the origin recovered immediately.\n- `cfg-782`/`cfg-783` are `cache=hit` `503 origin_timeout`, proving the failure was replayed from cache.\n\n**Changed files**\n\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/config-cache.mjs` — added a rejection handler that removes the cached entry on failure, but only if the map still points to the exact same in-flight promise. Successful entries are left untouched.\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/student-tests.mjs` — replaced the placeholder with three regression tests: failed load is removed and retried; concurrent waiters share the failure then a retry runs; and a late failure from a cleared/replaced load cannot evict the replacement.\n- `benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/INCIDENT.md` — completed the incident report.\n- `config-api.mjs` was not changed.\n\n**Verification**\n\n```bash\nnode --test benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/config-cache.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/student-tests.mjs\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```\nℹ tests 8\nℹ pass 8\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n**Remaining concern**\n\nUnder a persistent origin outage, every read will now trigger a fresh origin call because failures are never cached. This matches the required contract, but it means there is no internal backoff/circuit breaker. Operators should monitor origin health and use the existing `clear()` method if load becomes a problem."}],"usage":{"input_tokens":22689,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a57c6a4b-4261-4c82-8f24-11909ca7fa0e","uuid":"78a1dcc0-105e-4bf8-80c9-21be3c4f5192","timestamp":"2026-08-23T19:27:24.374Z"}
